Subject: [lilith-core-seam] Close failed turns without replay contamination

Persist a turn-scoped, redacted terminal boundary for provider failures so a
later model cannot inherit or replay the failed request. Large-context failures
rewind only when the marked user row is still the durable session head;
otherwise they close durably. Gateway recovery deduplicates only against the
exact returned turn marker and preserves terminal-error evidence.

Upstream base: 3c5fd918e3e2537cd74f4f88c990c5de5cbd9f63

